title: LSP Diagnostics - (Example)

Open this tiddler's `.tid` file in your editor and wait a moment for the warnings to settle. Only the first of these four lines is warned, as //No tiddler titled 'No Such Tiddler'//:

See [[No Such Tiddler]].

See [[LSP Server]].

Code `[[No Such Tiddler]]` here.

See [[docs|https://tiddlywiki.com]].

The second resolves. The third is inline code, which is not wikitext. The fourth is an external address, not a title.

Now add a link of your own to a title that does not exist, and watch the warning appear once you stop typing. Nothing needs saving: the server answers from the text in the editor.

Back to [[LSP Diagnostics]].
